# Review: MermaidPlugin

The plugin is one CodeMirror extension (`mermaid-extension.ts`) contributed through
`MarkdownCapabilities.ExtensionProvider`. It replaces each `mermaid` fence the cursor is outside of
with a block widget, shows the source while the cursor is inside (except in read-only), renders an
inline `cm-mermaid-error` on failure, follows the editor's dark-theme facet and paints the widget on
`--color-group-surface`. The behaviour largely matches; testing is thin. The only unit test checks
module activation, and four storybook stories (smoke-run by `ts-test-storybook`) render a flowchart, a
sequence diagram and an error case without asserting anything.

Divergences: the four types (`DiagramKind`, `DiagramTheme`, `RenderResult`, `RenderError`) are not
declared — the code uses mermaid's own `MermaidConfig`; `renderDiagram` is a private widget method
that turns every failure into a string rather than distinct parse and render errors; the source lines
are replaced by a block decoration, not hidden with a `cm-mermaid-hidden` class; and the module
activates on `MarkdownEvents.Start`, not `SetupExtensions`.

